/**
 * Flex known-answer vectors.
 *
 * GENERATED -- do not hand-edit.  See
 * the project notes
 *
 * flex_kat_header / flex_kat_expected
 * The end-to-end consensus vector, taken from the CPU reference
 * (cpuminer-opt algo/flex/flex-gate.c).  That pair came from a share a
 * live Flex/Kylacoin pool ACCEPTED, so it is consensus-correct by
 * construction.  flex_kat_header is the 80-byte header exactly as
 * flex_hash() receives it (be32enc'd work->data words); the digest reads
 * as little-endian words 0x0441f067 .. 0x00007a82.
 *
 * flex_sha3_* Independent SHA3 vectors, generated by Python's hashlib -- a
 * separate implementation of the 0x06 padding.  flex applies SHA3-style
 * padding to EVERY keccak in the chain (the selection seed, the KECCAK
 * core round at both 64 and 80 bytes, and the final SHA3-256), where this
 * tree's shared keccak code bakes in the legacy 0x01 byte.
 *
 * flex_keccak_* The SAME messages under legacy Keccak (0x01).  Baked in so a
 * padding mistake shows up as "you computed the 0x01 answer" rather than
 * as an anonymous mismatch.
 */

